{# What every agent reads at tool-discovery time, before it has written a single query.

   The opening line names the tools in the order they are used, and names them through
   `tool()` so that renaming one here without renaming it in `server.py` is a failing
   test rather than an instruction to call something that no longer exists.
#}
Search the user's own document collections in Hoover4.

Call {{ tool('list_collections') }} first so you use real collection names, then {{ tool('search_collections') }}
to find passages, then {{ tool('read_documents') }} to read them in full.
{% if has('cite_documents') %}

When you have the answer, call {{ tool('cite_documents') }} with the documents you relied on: it
returns a short handle for each, which you write into your prose where the claim is made.
{% endif %}

Use {{ tool('read_more') }} when a page contains a continuation. You can also use
{{ tool('search_facet_values') }}, {{ tool('search_date_histogram') }},
{{ tool('search_entity_explainer') }}, {{ tool('doc_sources') }}, {{ tool('doc_metadata') }},
{{ tool('doc_email') }}, {{ tool('doc_diff_sources') }}, {{ tool('pdf_search') }},
{{ tool('table_overview') }}, {{ tool('table_page') }}, {{ tool('table_column_values') }},
{{ tool('table_search_cells') }}, {{ tool('folder_overview') }}, {{ tool('folder_list') }},
and {{ tool('folder_search') }} for their named collection reads.

